                  Test for scheduling fairness

There are four components running on the same priority and two differnt CPUs
(two components on each CPU).

One of the components on CPU 0 has a single busy-looping thread whereas the
other component on CPU 0 releases a signal storm. The expected result is that
both, the entrypoint of the first component and the sender thread of the second
component et an equal share of the CPU.

The two components on the other CPU are busy-looping their entrypoint threads.
Moreover, one of those components has two busy-looping threads, the other has
two mutual exclusive threads. The expected result is that all busy-looping
threads shall receive an equal share of the CPU. The mutual exclusive threads
should get a bit less but a similar share.

